title: $:/plugins/nikorion/dyntable/language/en-GB/readme
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

\whitespace trim

Renders an editable, sortable, paginated HTML table from a filter — one row per tiddler, one column per field or data-index. Extracted from [[Shiraz|https://github.com/kookma/TW-Shiraz]]'s Dynamic Table feature as an independent plugin, with no dependency on Shiraz itself.

! Usage

```
<<dyntable filter:"[tag[task]]" fields:"title status priority due-date"/>>
```

! Parameters

|!Parameter |!Default |!Description |
|`filter` | |the source filter — one row per matching tiddler (required) |
|`fields` |`""` |space-separated field names, one column each |
|`indexes` |`""` |space-separated data-tiddler index names, one column each (use instead of `fields` when the source is a data tiddler — giving both, or neither, shows an error) |
|`sortType` |`"string"` |sort comparison used when a column header is clicked (`string`, `number`, `date`, …) |
|`caption` |`""` |wikitext rendered as the table caption |
|`class` |`""` |CSS class(es) applied to the `<table>` element |
|`footer` |`""` |computed footer rows, declared as a space-separated list of `calc[:decimals][@columns]` — see ''Footer calculations'' below |
|`footerRows` |`"0"` |number of hand-filled footer rows; in edit mode each footer cell is a text box whose wikitext is rendered in view mode within its column — type `<<sum>>`, `<<average>>`, `<<median>>`, `<<count>>`, `<<unique>>`, `<<product>>`, `<<range>>`, `<<minall>>`, `<<maxall>>` (optional argument = decimal places, e.g. `<<average 2>>`), or a plain English name such as `Sum` (shown translated). Cells are stored in `$:/keepstate/nikorion/dyntable/<stateTiddler>/footer` |
|`stateTiddler` |current tiddler |title used to key this table's state (sort, pagination, edit mode…) — set it when the same filter is rendered more than once on the same tiddler |
|`editButton` |`"yes"` |show the edit/view toggle button in the caption |
|`pagination` |`"no"` |paginate the rows instead of showing them all |
|`emptyMessage` |localised "filter input is empty" |wikitext shown when `filter` matches nothing |

! Footer calculations

`footer` adds one computed row per entry, with nothing to type in afterwards and nothing stored. Each entry is `calc[:decimals][@columns]`:

* `calc` — `sum`, `average`, `count`, `unique` (number of distinct values), `median`, `product`, `range` (max − min), `min` or `max`. The row label (Sum, Average…) is translated to the wiki language and shown in the first column, which is therefore never calculated.
* `:decimals` — optional number of decimal places, e.g. `average:1`.
* `@columns` — optional comma-separated columns to calculate, e.g. `sum@priority,grade`. Without it, the calculation applies to every column whose values are all numeric; other columns stay empty.

|!`calc` |!Label (en-GB) |!Result |
|`sum` |Sum |total of the values |
|`average` |Avg. |arithmetic mean |
|`count` |Val. count |number of values (one per row that has one) |
|`unique` |Unique val. count |number of distinct values (works on text too, with `@columns`) |
|`median` |Med. |middle value once sorted |
|`product` |Prod. |product of the values |
|`range` |Range |max − min |
|`min` |Min. |smallest value |
|`max` |Max. |largest value |

Labels are shown in bold serif followed by a colon (non-breaking space before it in French). Hovering a label shows a tooltip with the full name, then a short description of the calculation on a new line.

<<<
`<<dyntable filter:"[tag[Demo Task]]" fields:"title priority" footer:"sum average:1 max">>`
<<<

Which calculation? The ''average'' suits steady values where the total matters (monthly expenses). The ''median'' (middle value once sorted) suits skewed values, where a few extremes would drag the average (resolution times, salaries). For a reliable picture show both plus the extremes: `footer:"average:1 median:1 min max"`. A large gap between average and median reveals skewed values; with very few values, or two distinct groups, the median alone can mislead.

As the value is a plain string, a footer definition can be reused like any other value: `footer={{Preset!!footer}}`, `footer=<<totals>>` (after `\define totals() sum average:1`) or `footer={{{ [[Preset]get[footer]] }}}`. Computed rows come first, then the `footerRows` ones if both are given.

! Column templates

A column's rendering is looked up by field/index name against tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/nk-Table/HeaderTemplate`, `$:/tags/nk-Table/BodyTemplate` and `$:/tags/nk-Table/FooterTemplate`, matched on their `tbl-column-list` field, falling back to `templates/header|body|footer/default`. Built-in templates cover `title`, `type`, `tags`, `color`, `email`, `created`/`modified`, and the task-manager fields `priority`, `status`, `role`, `maturity`, `due-date`, plus action columns `tbl-checkbox`, `tbl-clone`, `tbl-delete`, `tbl-expand`, `tbl-nodetype`/`tbl-linktype`. The `project` field has no dedicated template: it's free text, so it falls back to the generic `default` (editable text) and only gets a column label. Add your own by tagging a tiddler with the matching template tag and a `tbl-column-list` field.

The `role`, `maturity` and `status` columns rely on [[TW-Base-Fields|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-Base-Fields]]'s controlled vocabulary (`$:/plugins/nikorion/base-fields/vocab/<field>`): icon, label and optional grouping (for `role`) come from that plugin, never stored in the field. Without TW-Base-Fields installed, these three columns stay blank rather than erroring. A record whose `status` is `done` gets the `tbl-record-complete` class on its row (text coloured pale green, theme-aware; the title column keeps its normal colours). `dropped` greys the row's text; `paused` gets no styling but keeps the `tbl-record-paused` class.

To hide some tags from the `tags` column, define an `sv-exclude-tags` variable holding a filter around the table, e.g. `<$let sv-exclude-tags="[[Demo Task]] [prefix[$:/]]"><<dyntable ...>></$let>`.

! Localisation

Every label, tooltip and message follows the wiki language (`en-GB` and `fr-FR` shipped, falling back to `en-GB`). Column headers show the label found under `$:/plugins/nikorion/dyntable/language/<lang>/Tables/Column/<name>` — shipped for `title`, `text`, `caption`, `type`, `created`, `modified`, `creator`, `modifier`, `color`, `email`, `priority`, `status`, `role`, `maturity`, `project`, `due-date` — and otherwise the raw field/index name: `tags` and your own fields display as is. To label a custom column, create a tiddler with that title, e.g. `$:/plugins/nikorion/dyntable/language/fr-FR/Tables/Column/budget` containing `Budget`.

Priority values and link types are translated the same way (`Tables/Priority/<value>`, `Tables/NodeType/<type>`); the values stored in the fields stay canonical, so switching the language never alters your data. `role`, `maturity` and `status` values are translated by TW-Base-Fields instead (see above). Any cell holding a TiddlyWiki date (17 digits, e.g. `created`, `modified` or a custom field) or an ISO date (`2026-09-20`, as typed in a date input) is shown with the [[date format|https://tiddlywiki.com/#DateFormat]] in `Tables/Format/Date`, whatever the column name; editing still shows the stored value.

! Settings

The record editor used in expanded/edit mode (simple text box vs. the main TiddlyWiki editor) is configurable from the ''Table'' tab in the control panel.

! Styling the table (`class=`)

`class=` on `<<dyntable>>` takes any CSS class, including the Bootstrap-style utility classes shipped by [[Shiraz|https://github.com/kookma/TW-Shiraz]] (`styles/bs/`) or, without Shiraz, by [[TW-Tiny-Bootstrap|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-Tiny-Bootstrap]] alone (same classes, self-disables if Shiraz is present — so if both are installed, Shiraz's own CSS wins and Tiny Bootstrap stays inactive).

|!Group |!Example classes |!What it does |
|Sizing |`w-100`, `w-50`, `h-auto` |width/height as a % of the container, or `auto` |
|Spacing |`m-3`, `mt-0`, `p-2`, `gap-1` |margin/padding/gap on a 0–5 scale |
|Borders |`border`, `border-primary`, `border-2` |add a border, colour it, set its thickness |
|Rounded corners |`rounded`, `rounded-circle`, `rounded-pill` |round the corners of elements inside a cell (images, badges…); no effect on the `<table>` itself (`border-collapse`) |
|Text / background colour |`text-danger`, `bg-success-subtle`, `text-bg-warning` |semantic colours (primary, success, danger…), full or "subtle" strength |
|Text alignment / effects |`text-center`, `text-truncate`, `text-uppercase` |align, truncate with an ellipsis, change case |
|Shadows / float |`shadow-sm`, `float-end`, `clearfix` |drop shadow, float a cell/element, clear floats |

Full class list: TW-Tiny-Bootstrap's [[readme|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-Tiny-Bootstrap]] or the [[Bootstrap 5.3 utility docs|https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/]].

Table-specific variants ship built into this plugin (no dependency), ported from Shiraz's `styles/tables.css`:

|!Class |!What it does |
|`table-hover` |highlight the row under the mouse |
|`table-hover-yellow`, `table-hover-cyan` |same, with a yellow/cyan highlight instead |
|`table-striped-row` |alternate row background colour |
|`table-striped-col` |alternate column background colour |
|`table-borderless` |remove all cell borders |
|`table-lines` |horizontal rule under each row only, footer rows included (combine with `table-borderless`) |
|`table-sides` |vertical rules on the far left and far right of the body rows only (combine with `table-borderless`) |
|`table-center` |center the table in its container |
|`table-caption-top` |move the caption above the table instead of below |
|`table-tight` |smaller font size |
|`table-rounded`, `table-rounded-0` … `table-rounded-5` |round the outer corners of the table — header, and last footer row (or last row without a footer); the rounding only shows where the cells have a background, so colour the header and footer with `thead-*` and `tfoot-*`; borders stay square, so combine with `table-borderless`, e.g. `class="table-borderless thead-dark tfoot-dark table-rounded-3"`. Sizes of Bootstrap's `rounded-1` … `rounded-5`; the Bootstrap `rounded` classes do nothing on a table |
|`thead-primary`, `thead-secondary`, `thead-success`, `thead-warning`, `thead-danger`, `thead-info`, `thead-dark`, `thead-light` |colour the header row |
|`tfoot-primary`, `tfoot-secondary`, `tfoot-success`, `tfoot-warning`, `tfoot-danger`, `tfoot-info`, `tfoot-dark`, `tfoot-light` |colour the footer rows (same palette as `thead-*`; shown when `footer` or `footerRows` is used) |

! Compatibility

Safe to install alongside Shiraz: internal procedures are tagged `$:/tags/nk-Table/*` (own namespace, imported via `[all[shadows+tiddlers]tag[...]]`), separate from Shiraz's own `$:/tags/Table/*` — no more shared tags, so no duplicate/conflicting definitions, on top of the already-separate macro name (`<<dyntable>>` vs. Shiraz's `<<table-dynamic>>`), tiddler titles, CSS classes and state/config namespace (`$:/config/nikorion/dyntable/…`, `$:/state/nikorion/dyntable`, `$:/keepstate/nikorion/dyntable`). Installing both lets `class=` on `<<dyntable>>` pick up Shiraz's Bootstrap-style utility classes.

Optional plugins used if present, ignored otherwise: [[TW-Math|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-Math]] (numeric cells and computed `footer` values are rendered through `<$math>`, so they follow its settings: KaTeX, decimal separator, notation, precision — max 6 decimals by default), [[TW-Trashbin|https://github.com/kookma/TW-Trashbin]] (delete moves records to trash instead of deleting permanently), [[TW-Pikaday|https://github.com/kookma/TW-Pikaday]] (date picker on `due-date` columns).

! Requirements

TiddlyWiki >= 5.3.5.
